{%- comment -%}
  Private to Hotspot; explicitly targeted there and nowhere else.

  Product card — the price.

  **The figure is the price of the variant the button posts**, which is what
  `snippets/card-option.liquid` resolves: Shopify's selected or first available
  variant. The displayed figure and submitted variant therefore always agree.

  **The tax note is a sibling, not part of this element**, and that is the
  reason it can be a block at all. `theme.js` replaces this element's whole
  `innerHTML` on an option pick, so anything rendered inside it would be wiped
  by the first control click. Out here a sibling is never touched,
  which is the arrangement the quick view already uses: "the note is a sibling
  of the figure, so a pick rewrites the figure's own text node and the note is
  never touched."
{%- endcomment -%}

{% render 'card-price', product: closest.product, show_unit_price: false, attributes: block.shopify_attributes %}

